{"schema_version":2,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:35-14","provision":"BCO 35-14","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"35-14","title":"Section 35-14","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/35-14/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/35-14","current_text":{"html":"<p>An officer or private member of the church refusing to testify may be censured for contumacy.</p>","text":"An officer or private member of the church refusing to testify may be censured for contumacy."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"f8bde72b35f9475713a5751081d525f119bc6b4daf3b43ddc86694065015654b","parent_id":"bco:35","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":5,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:35-14--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-04.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-04.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Biese et al. v. Tennessee Valley Presbytery","year":2024,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-04.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-04.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:35-14--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-04.md:occ-3734a5d216ea","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-04.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-04.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-04.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["Sabbath observance","Super Bowl party","review and control","session records review","SJC jurisdiction","exception of substance","Westminster Confession 21:8","WLC 117","WLC 118","BCO 40-2","BCO 40-3","non-justiciability","adjacent courts","RAO Chapter 16"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2023-4"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Biese and others complained that Tennessee Valley Presbytery erred by approving Redeemer Church session minutes without exception—minutes noting a youth Super Bowl party—and by denying their complaint seeking a Sabbath exception. The SJC denied the complaint: because Presbytery gave no reasons for its actions, the record was insufficient to find it erred in interpreting the Constitution. A concurrence said the denial did not decide the Sabbath merits; a dissent would have held the complaint judicially out of order for lack of SJC jurisdiction over presbytery record review."}},{"id":"bco:35-14--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-19.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-19.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Huffman v. Tennessee Valley Presbytery","year":2024,"disposition":"other","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-19.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-19.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:35-14--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-19.md:occ-dd3da350b1ed","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-19.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-19.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-19.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["BCO 38-1 case without process","retroactive application of amended BCO","complaint vs. appeal","confession of sin","judicially out of order","remand","50th General Assembly BCO amendment"],"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2023-19"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"A filing challenging Presbytery’s handling of Huffman’s BCO 38-1 confession was styled as an appeal under a newly amended rule. The SJC found it judicially out of order because the case began and was nearly completed when the former rule provided review by complaint, and retroactive application would be unfair. It remanded for Presbytery to adjudicate the filing as a complaint at its next stated meeting; denial or failure to act permits review by the SJC. No merits issue was decided."}},{"id":"bco:35-14--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-06_2023-08.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-06_2023-08.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Knox Baird et al. v. Grace Presbytery","year":2024,"disposition":"partially_sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-06_2023-08.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-06_2023-08.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:35-14--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-06_2023-08.md:occ-b2eb2d50de23","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-06_2023-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-06_2023-08.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":330},"excerpt":"charges, could form the basis for further action by the court. See BCO 35-14.","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-06_2023-08.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["complaint procedure","BCO 40-5 review","document production","stay of judicial proceedings","mootness"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2023-8"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Case 2023-08 was adjudicated with Case 2023-06 in the Baird complaints against Grace Presbytery. The SJC sustained the complaints in the main, rejected one specification, and did not reach another; concurring opinions were recorded."}},{"id":"bco:35-14--case:cases/ga49_2022__2020-14.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga49_2022__2020-14.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Myers v. Illiana Presbytery","year":2022,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga49_2022__2020-14.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga49_2022__2020-14.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:35-14--case:cases/ga49_2022__2020-14.md:occ-44d6faa54110","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga49_2022__2020-14.html","repository_path":"cases/ga49_2022__2020-14.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":49},"excerpt":"<table><tbody><tr><td>10/31/20</td><td>After Commission deliberation, the Defendant was</td></tr><tr><td>unanimously found guilty of the charge of &quot;maltreatment of</td></tr><tr><td>his wife&quot; and the charge of “fits of anger&quot;.</td></tr><tr><td>11","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga49_2022__2020-14.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["maltreatment of wife","fits of anger","hearsay evidence","eyewitness requirement","BCO 32-20 statute of limitations","pastoral care vs. judicial process","new evidence","indefinite suspension"],"case_numbers":["2020-14"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"TE Aaron Myers appealed his conviction on charges of maltreatment of his wife and fits of anger by Illiana Presbytery; the SJC denied the appeal and upheld all four specifications of error arguments raised by the appellant, affirming the indefinite suspension from office and suspension from the sacraments."}},{"id":"bco:35-14--case:cases/ga24_1996__1995-01.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga24_1996__1995-01.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"David C. Lachman v. Philadelphia Presbytery","year":1995,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga24_1996__1995-01.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga24_1996__1995-01.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:35-14--case:cases/ga24_1996__1995-01.md:occ-9a301fc9a3ea","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga24_1996__1995-01.html","repository_path":"cases/ga24_1996__1995-01.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":130},"excerpt":"earlier judgment. BCO 35-14 and 42-5. This process does honor to the concept that","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga24_1996__1995-01.md"},{"id":"bco:35-14--case:cases/ga24_1996__1995-01.md:occ-77dad3aa36ad","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga24_1996__1995-01.html","repository_path":"cases/ga24_1996__1995-01.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":133},"excerpt":"and adjudicate the matter. BCO 35-14 and 42-5. Since the lower court is always a party","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga24_1996__1995-01.md"}],"metadata":{"case_numbers":["1995-1"],"body":"SJC/CJB"}}],"history":[{"kind":"change","year":1996,"ga":24,"note":"The indexed BCO change record names 35-14.","url":"markdown/ga24_1996.md","status":"section named in extracted change meta